  T("The criticism. After the preprint, commentators noted that the first match gave Stockfish little hash memory, a fixed time per move that denied its time management, and no opening book or endgame tablebase, and that the hardware was not comparable. DeepMind answered in the Science paper with 1000 games under conditions like the TCEC superfinal, on 44 threads and 32 GB of hash with tablebases, and also tried openings from human games and time-odds matches. The result held, +155 -6 =839, and Stockfish needed about ten to one time odds to match AlphaZero, according to the reports."),
